        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update the content lint workflow to print the linted merge commit and a hint to merge <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> when linting fails.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Make it easier to understand lint failures caused by combining the PR with newer changes on <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>, which don't reproduce on the PR branch.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The workflow lints <code class=\"notranslate\">refs/pull/&lt;n&gt;/merge</code>. In <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5183803738\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45225\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45225/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45225\">#45225</a>, <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> had meanwhile gained its own <code class=\"notranslate\">named-feature()</code> section, so the merge result contained a duplicate heading (MD024 on line 173) that didn't exist in the PR branch.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Relates to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5183803738\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45225\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45225/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45225\">#45225</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46571",
            "title": "ci(pr-check-lint_content): print linted merge + base-branch hint on failure",
            "date_modified": "2026-11-18T12:18:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-11-17T17:51:01.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added pages for the following commands of the <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#navigation\" rel=\"nofollow\">Navigation</a> chapter of WebDriver Classic:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Get Current URL</li>\n<li>Navigate To</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Spec links</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#navigate-to\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#navigate-to</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#get-current-url\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#get-current-url</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Compat quirks worth looking into:</h3>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Chrome</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Navigate To and invalid certificates.</strong> With <code class=\"notranslate\">acceptInsecureCerts</code> set to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code>, navigating to a page with a self-signed certificate returned <code class=\"notranslate\">null</code> and loaded the \"Privacy error\" interstitial, where the spec returns <code class=\"notranslate\">insecure certificate</code> (seen in my test run, headless and headed). BCD shows Navigate To as supported since Chrome 65 with no note about this.</li>\n<li><strong>Outdated <code class=\"notranslate\">w3c</code> note.</strong> BCD's Chrome entries for both commands say to include <code class=\"notranslate\">{\"goog:chromeOptions\": {\"w3c\": true}}</code> in the capabilities. My test sessions didn't set it, and both commands returned W3C responses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">/cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/sadym-chromium/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/sadym-chromium\">@sadym-chromium</a> for the BCD update.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46570",
            "title": "[Technical review] Add WebDriver Classic Navigate To and Get Current URL pages",
            "date_modified": "2026-11-17T16:41:45.000Z",
